  "full_file_asr_raw": "Matt, on September 6th, Holden Sherman was writing about Common Malwatch taking a larger role. Five days later, Phoenix announced Mark Williams' shoulder surgery. The young players may now get their chance sooner. Camp will help show how much of their preparation carries into dependable play. The team has yet to establish a return timetable for Williams. Malwatch averaged 19.5 points and nearly 13 rebounds across four summer league games in July. He gave people a reason to be interested. Camp and preseason will begin to show how much of that carries into a larger role. The public sees only part of the preparation. As the young players take on more responsibility, their performances will give ownership a better sense of where that work is paying off and where they still need time. In the Suns' discussion thread reviewed after the injury, some supporters welcomed an opportunity for the young players. Others asked for patience. Those reactions came from one self-selected conversation. They give a directional view of the expectations forming around the group. Media Day is Monday, September 28th. Training camp starts the next day, Tuesday, September 29th. Specific accounts of a player's preparation at Media Day would give people something to follow as the games begin. The league scan includes the Clippers' penalties and their effects on future roster options and current leadership. Toronto is still waiting for the reported Kawhi Leonard trade to be completed. The league's 60-game NBA TV schedule is also out. That completes the national television package and gives Phoenix the full schedule for assessing its exposure. For Phoenix, the encouraging outcome would be seeing young players become dependable in larger roles. Contributions that hold up across games would tell the organization more about the depth it has been building. Much love, my brother. Dominate. Dominate. Dominate. Dominate. Dominate. Dominate.",
  "final_ten_seconds_asr": "dependable in larger roles. Contributions that hold up across games will tell the organization more about the depth it has been building. Much love, my brother. Dominate."
